dem-paragraph.gls -- dem-paragraph.txt

The file: one paragraph of 50,000 words on one line (345 KB).

Open:   chezweb dem-paragraph.txt

1. M-q                   Expect: some 5,000 lines of at most 70 columns,
                         within 2 s (1.3 to 1.9 s in the cloud: close to
                         the limit).
2. M-<  M-q              Expect: the same text (nothing to change), within
                         2 s (it did not end in minutes before 22 November
                         2026).
3. C-x C-w /tmp/dem-paragraph-filled.txt RET
   In a terminal:
     tr -s ' \n' '\n\n' < dem-paragraph.txt > /tmp/a
     tr -s ' \n' '\n\n' < /tmp/dem-paragraph-filled.txt > /tmp/b
     cmp /tmp/a /tmp/b
   Expect: no output (every word kept, in order).
4. C-/                   Expect: the one line back.  The buffer is marked
                         changed again (* on the mode line), and stays so:
                         since step 3 the file on disk is the filled text,
                         and the buffer no longer is.  More C-/ say "No
                         further undo information" (M-q was the only
                         change).  Emacs does the same.
5. C-x k RET, then "y" or "yes" when it asks about the unsaved changes:
   they are not to be saved (/tmp/dem-paragraph-filled.txt keeps the
   filled text).
